# LF in the working copy on every OS, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# The generators and vendor checks compare files byte for byte. With autocrlf, a Windows checkout
# is CRLF while the scripts write LF, so `gen-tokens --check`, `gen-icons --check` and the vendor
# checks failed on a clean checkout, and running a generator showed every file it touched as
# modified with no content change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party code is kept byte for byte as its package ships it: the vendor scripts hash
# it against node_modules, and any conversion would read as a hand edit.
src/Dray.Ui/wwwroot/lib/** -text
